  "identity": "A warm 6/8 memory-song: every bar spans three quarter-note beats, felt as two dotted-quarter pulses. A repeated D opening leaps to A, then folds back through F-sharp and E like a wave remembering the shore. Nylon-guitar articulation and a rounded grand-piano lead alternate breathing space with small sixteenth-note recollections. D-major warmth shades into B minor; descending bass, not distortion or a rock crescendo, carries the emotional weight. Hook and peak use the chorus harmony; the solo also follows the eight-bar chorus progression. The peak answers the hook conversationally rather than doubling it at the octave. Upper notes are isolated quiet responses, never a second continuous lead. Let the final D finish at beat two and leave the remaining quarter-beat unit silent.",
